# Self-interest trigger, activated by this package's own postinst.
#
# It exists to move the service start to the END of the dpkg run. Two reasons,
# both measured on a from-scratch install:
#
#   * dh_installinit emits its `invoke-rc.d drumee-server-pod start` BEFORE
#     dh_installsystemd's block, which is where the unit is first enabled — and
#     nothing does a daemon-reload in between. On a genuinely fresh install
#     systemd does not yet know the unit, so invoke-rc.d silently does nothing
#     and returns 0. The install reports success and the stack is down.
#   * drumee-ui-pod depends on drumee-server-pod, so dpkg configures the UI
#     AFTER it. Starting the server from its own postinst therefore starts a
#     stack whose UI is not in place yet.
#
# dpkg runs triggered maintainer scripts once every other package in the
# transaction is configured, which is exactly when the stack can come up.
interest-noawait drumee-server-pod-start
